 17592186378045}] :question/id #uuid "35c7bb5a-6cc2-546e-bf03-4a857a7223ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-95202" :question/problem "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the plane whose parametric equation is $r=sv+tw$, where\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nNotice that the plane $r=sv+tw$ is actually the subspace $\\text{Span}{v,w}.$ \nHence, we have \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}{(\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{21}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -8 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 17 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fa4c46e-c82a-5404-add0-e946f7c95409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #ed