{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d71454-0458-5173-92e2-d24ae7d33b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420761} {:answer/id #uuid "299c3fa6-9fa8-5565-8634-09054fedc6f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420762} {:answer/id #uuid "48db3d3c-30c7-55ab-a903-b5f38c30500f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420768} {:answer/id #uuid "96fb9c14-df10-5b90-9b22-46eaa98a547f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420777} {:answer/id #uuid "f34f3108-25b4-52ad-8686-5c2f57c96aad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420777} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce23d7e-7b89-51d8-91ae-2e6f5b73477c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420788}] :question/id #uuid "f7a5359f-8967-570a-b634-daaee8dbc9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-138535" :question/problem "$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & 0 & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c000fb-0f6e-5949-8db6-c4c5d28b3248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432587} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe77835-4c02-5a54-960e-f2c670d5fae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432589} {:answer/id #uuid "8e69fde6-984a-5a8b-8dd0-63b58423f006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432591} {:answer/id #uuid "afeacb94-4e5b-58cc-be9f-c0b7884171f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432592} {:answer/id #uuid "c0338917-af25-5f02-ba7d-b2159df253f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432591} :answer-field/id #uuid "2881387b-754e-56f3-834a-ac7d858e2ecf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432596}] :question/id #uuid "3fcee73d-521b-5fd0-a9c6-c7b6d8e05cce" :question/math-academy-id "q-138516" :question/problem "$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c592a0-a31a-5768-80a4-19414e8114d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510785} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca7b07c-b688-5430-bb51-a1a02662d23f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510921} {:answer/id #uuid "503b74e3-9bce-5949-8ad7-9b878630cf87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510953} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9aa926-113d-59e6-8eab-0e2641ef958e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511144} {:answer/id #uuid "caa6eda2-e6f0-5988-9e38-f7cffa0af3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511144} :answer-field/id #uuid "29dc167c-c1ad-5d54-8910-071c51c74e87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511334}] :question/id #uuid "80fca04e-db43-5719-819a-d2aec209a00e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138536" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pseudoinverse of a Matrix Given Its Singular Value Decomposition"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162090 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161903 :question/id #uuid "64e7f84f-da34-5ae2-b2d1-72373a1d2888" :question/math-academy-id "e-9829" :question/problem "For the matrix \n![](images/1d/1d0733f2c724253c804c596e1d0a1432b8281afa7a14a9dc6702b099ab4795e0.svg) find the pseudoinverse $A^+.$" :question/worked-solution "For an \"almost\" zero $m \\times n$ matrix with non-zero entries \n\n$$\n\\sigma_1, \\: \\sigma_2, \\: \\ldots, \\: \\sigma_r\n$$\n\non the main diagonal, the corresponding pseudoinverse is the \"almost\" zero $n \\times m$ matrix with entries \n\n$$\n{\\sigma_1^{-1}}, \\, {\\sigma_2^{-1}}, \\, \\ldots, \\, {\\sigma_r^{-1}}\n$$\n\non the main diagonal.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{+} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{6}^{-1} & \\,\\,\\,0 & 0 \\\\ \\,\\,0 & \\,{4}^{-1} & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3460bfd6-8b2f-5a52-891a-4c8b2af5b5e8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid