A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c473f5-ef95-5227-a968-e2e86ab24e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463640} {:answer/id #uuid "ef280a56-6aa4-5367-afd4-c488c98b4baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce7c6c8-b9b1-552a-b5e1-0f6140ff2c88" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464754} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "929235db-049d-563d-9c46-3e63d1f2cabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9297a7-d7f3-5f84-9db4-8e4456568e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} :answer-field/id #uuid "48fb156a-09ce-5fde-8695-5588211123e1" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464755} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb27b827-2491-5ec9-8772-7e647962fd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463644} {:answer/id #uuid "da00eb55-ba67-5112-89f2-1681a8d1c68d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd2d553-3e6c-5d1d-9ac4-1a5aba1b575d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464756}] :question/id #uuid "2e8059f3-ef63-587d-911b-0d0c0a784873" :question/math-academy-id "q-127755" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f57cf2ee-5c54-5728-9819-04ba25ccaed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe95562-995d-540a-a75b-c6729affad85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} :answer-field/id #uuid "09b46ce7-eeb0-59a8-90f1-679f8c0295ff" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde6b23b-b56d-5b3d-a341-8a7675217e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463648} {:answer/id #uuid "306399cf-a4fb-5e1f-9e1c-fab262184a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b22761-b532-55a6-93c3-281e6baeea2e" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad303f4b-49e7-5eb1-b038-2436daaa6d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3babfc-5f8a-55a0-949b-758d8eacf432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7b1f0e4-c9c9-5321-988b-aaf8e81cba4d" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464759}] :question/id #uuid "87b20497-ceac-5d64-8634-616821707ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127757" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30b47ef-87b0-5e27-a184-0a096fd33124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463652} {:answer/id #uuid "33d939ee-6d35-51bf-8bb9-1d48cd53e796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f6015b-077b-5764-a2dd-d3aae8b43612" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af08d0a-5536-510f-abab-da5fdbdceb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463654} {:answer/id #uuid "35d0cb07-478b-566b-9247-784f753b25b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463654} :answer-field/id #uuid "dedfc344-69b8-5863-a5ce-c4f18d91df8a" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9ccb9cb-9df6-55dc-8aff-1d3a958bab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463656} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec3ad4b-8ef7-53f9-a9d2-9dabd3a7a706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463657} :answer-field/id #uuid "189a8dad-81d9-534b-b8f8-9df3343a27e3" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464762}] :question/id #uuid "c7dc44ce-440a-5f50-b6a8-db3db16e9582" :question/math-academy-id "q-127762" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 3=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=4\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 12=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc10acc5-cbe4-5aa7-85e8-9d27a5cfe577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463658} {:answer/id #uuid "54ce08b8-b1b6-51d3-82c5-8ce0eae6a5df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463659} :answer-field/id #uuid "8037c49c-f8b0-55ab-9b8d-c0cab9f33665" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f65a48c6-d48a-5389-9967-5b20a96b30f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463660} {:answer/id #uuid "839aeca5-60b3-587e-9712-cc3955ffe0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463660} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae8dfdf-3ddf-57c5-b5be-6a6ce59947b9" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f467b224-40ff-5b05-86f0-3f8c1a836859" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463662} {:answer/id #uuid "efd8deea-90c9-5a2d-8712-50eac0029e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463662} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bc783cb-7e9c-5966-ba24-f9cc38ab506c" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464765}] :question/id #uuid "7be51f92-4cc3-51a8-b911-c18f52c55601" :question/math-academy-id "q-127821" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd7bbbf-6e0c-51c5-a9fa-fc0f2bf1d945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467896} {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afb67d1-8168-5df5-930f-8190b07edc62" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fa4bf8-f217-5274-8dab-28c162bb278d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467898} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00bd3e1-111e-5780-871b-467da013e81a" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} {:answer/id #uuid "906cb48c-7d29-5136-a248-2c29457a1fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c5cafc-4559-5564-a3f4-1bb51c7edb62" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468671}] :question/id #uuid "6118feb2-c751-599a-b3b9-c8c760c49b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71934" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04e9358-9109-5802-a83d-c003136f6776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467902} {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b39826b-4d43-597b-b35d-5dd3a91ceaf8" :answer-field/key "X" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6c71b-66a8-52d7-88ab-87e3a0607923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f838e05-1a03-57ee-8f9c-10a9e960bcdd" :answer-field/key "Y" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62048c-e540-5983-8cbf-aabcf18ff59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2386ffd6-0069-5a17-ae65-0bf5f760c977" :answer-field/key "Z" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468674}] :question/id #uuid "f09c20fa-fbe3-5a9f-8218-d2a4dd2af13c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dd891b-d694-5499-8817-937a44eceff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} {:answer/id #uuid "d5955946-ccfb-5755-8612-e0cdabb5eab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468238} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a54a548-43f3-5af9-bb27-c37157e1ba17" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91fda060-34cb-56bf-a286-798cf5974bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468240} {:answer/id #uuid "691d2f9b-6944-52d3-b95e-6577e5ed9262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468241} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1dfcd78-f8c3-5201-b805-25717f44d7c0" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44aed856-5960-53b9-88e1-18229b5f5d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} {:answer/id #uuid "cbda35bc-2510-530d-8b17-8fd2a72ea3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468242} :answer-field/id #uuid "121ad5e6-2d71-5c46-b7a0-42914d3db890" :answer-field/key "G" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468842}] :question/id #uuid "6cd97c58-6193-5fe7-8948-41d6f4bfcd71" :question/math-academy-id "q-7923" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,G=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $D$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(D)=3\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(D)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $D$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $F$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(F)=6\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(F)=0,$ we conclude that $F$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $G$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(G)=(-2)\\cdot 4-4\\cdot 2=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(G)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $G$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ does not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "741083d8-7378-5329-81bd-75ee950b2144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471555} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7d78d5-2816-585a-9205-a6e70044ec0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471556} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec26382-ce45-51fe-9719-373d673b7f62" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3df8f3cc-d84c-5eee-b203-2e5b3a76ac8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471557} {:answer/id #uuid "084c65aa-a350-580e-b2a3-5201f6c81dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471558} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2cbff6b-6444-5254-a29c-7df2a40ce247" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "699ee824-9041-5440-9507-9d2a68088e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471559} {:answer/id #uuid "b999e8b9-c8e3-57fc-af6a-5cfb661ee0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471559} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a76c867-cf40-5ba2-9a8c-90664e519511" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472285}] :question/id #uuid "17761662-c8e1-5053-be1d-f17ca1632a52" :question/math-academy-id "q-7915" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba324b7-0f59-5f58-97d8-72603006234e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472568} {:answer/id #uuid "35d1bf70-dd44-5f00-ace4-811a4e3e1bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472569} :answer-field/id #uuid "70d07d03-c34c-5845-8935-896ff2fde738" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6761343e-3cb3-55f7-a59d-31304c33661b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472570} {:answer/id #uuid "b1649aac-77b0-5dac-9373-2f007c41a012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472570} :answer-field/id #uuid "6588ae30-e559-5601-8ef8-17cc3ef6f0a1" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5499f975-6325-5729-a9ba-045a3cca2d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472572} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc00b66-d40e-52ef-8970-33efae0b0fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472572} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cced4e2-6cfd-5a39-854d-313251047edc" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473681}] :question/id #uuid "dd3729c7-43c0-5883-808f-5b63c7f7af84" :question/math-academy-id "q-127826" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bba5ddca-29ae-5471-a6a4-993be5c996d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473266} {:answer/id #uuid "8369e458-effb-5b2b-b5d4-aba006c45804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473267} :answer-field/id #uuid "8863fa22-3b39-5e93-9963-14e8b851c92e" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60e26ea5-9f10-529e-82c8-1409cac8b2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473268} {:answer/id #uuid "1749b0ec-a540-5a67-a5c4-d23285285ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473268} :answer-field/id #uuid "de8378a0-44cf-5391-92e6-89fe38fdd15b" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e75c4be-b101-5f9d-baaf-856e7cc7d65f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473270} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e2e004-d50b-5230-b52c-79e97034086b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473270} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce016b55-73ba-587f-8f45-40784a020589" :answer-field/key "Z" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474030}] :question/id #uuid "5f5bb9d1-db59-54f4-aa53-0a0fa0a6f6c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-71935" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nN=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $N$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(N)=3\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(N)=0,$ we conclude that $N$ is not invertible. Since $N$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $N$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $V$ is a $5\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 8=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1be0fb0-9847-565b-b3c1-581466264ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473272} {:answer/id #uuid "037b4724-2974-5573-821c-be931e428675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473272} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f2a2ea-24ce-5a7c-a465-8a604fac4939" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af46807b-2810-56be-88f8-06e3ecb337ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473274} {:answer/id #uuid "238549e7-3ff3-56c2-b10d-990ab4747696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473274} :answer-field/id #uuid "b73a784d-7afb-5d08-b1c6-524d553bcf9d" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c234f526-26f2-5eb0-a6cf-173562472af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473276} {:answer/id #uuid "aaad2947-e803-5417-9079-e397f4a8ca24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473277} :answer-field/id #uuid "775f56d7-7a83-56b8-89ed-384ecac6070a" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474033}] :question/id #uuid "ff070848-777f-5635-9918-6da54f4ec8b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-71937" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=3\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-15)=-3.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $V$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(V)=6\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(V)=0,$ we conclude that $V$ is not invertible. Since $V$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $V$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $V$ is singular."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087703 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087510 :question/id #uuid "ef06dd89-501b-5d2b-a56d-4554a049a91d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4504" :question/problem "If \n$\\begin{bmatrix}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{bmatrix}$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a320573-387a-58d0-a0b4-fdc4235e8e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084675} {:answer/id #uuid "b777fb43-93d7-5dc7-a4cd-7e540ebf1199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = ± 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084676} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2c3fcb-2ccc-509d-8f4e-73dfead21b8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = ± 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084677} {:answer/id #uuid "f2eeec69-0a0d-5c28-bc9b-bdbb673c7f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084678} {:answer/id #uuid "084389ec-184e-56fd-a7b7-39ad8aa9eec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084679}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b584fe55-a8c9-57cf-9bbb-cda45a7e1807" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084674}] :question/id #uuid "f2b7dccf-26ea-59f4-bdf6-7d70d461f4e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11722" :question/problem "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}k & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "419dd4e5-12cc-5539-9ce1-12dbb328e826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251098} {:answer/id #uuid "7e26377c-0b5f-5e88-8cee-a0c378d66f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251612} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d02b22-933b-5127-9e49-db343d3d3057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251946} {:answer/id #uuid "e9173fd7-88e5-5605-babf-0c1896274065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252591} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a703d4-42c5-5789-b2d3-b2087a71eba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251946} :answer-field/id #uuid "73272f9c-f427-56d0-a21e-b2927edff5b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253010}] :question/id #uuid "ee61babb-f6b1-5a98-9886-55df60a724bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-11723" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k & k \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot 1-k\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =k-2k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =0 \\\\ k & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097794a2-c7ca-5ecf-bd92-2d6b9637edf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} {:answer/id #uuid "87862fd4-0b9f-5398-911d-63cce6d1b136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251692} {:answer/id #uuid "c745fe31-0cba-5f79-a40c-985ece6242bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252314} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e5419b-2e45-5470-ad3f-325c6e4e71dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252419} {:answer/id #uuid "e279ed19-5a71-5d13-9f8d-6703bfc76869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} :answer-field/id #uuid "886a0983-97da-5781-96e9-27635821fd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253038}] :question/id #uuid "18e87006-2d52-52b3-8fdf-cef524aa5a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11719" :question/problem "If $F=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57d016cc-b32a-556a-872a-d9d9454755e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251269} {:answer/id #uuid "7f24ab14-2022-5d0d-aa61-084ff480fc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251621} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0e0abc-a204-57f0-a0ca-d651601dc526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} {:answer/id #uuid "e207ec5b-404c-50f6-acae-784dfe8e282b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252541} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fa13d3-a4d7-5bb5-8a44-96e5e778acbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e9e596-1625-5316-9294-354fbe58edae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253103}] :question/id #uuid "e6398e19-0166-5ea2-9ff8-a93fab46629b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11721" :question/problem "If $Q=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ x & x\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783db2fd-7825-5c2a-a37c-ecf12e9a46b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251550} {:answer/id #uuid "78c0bab0-9b03-5269-8dab-8e7ea4106e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} {:answer/id #uuid "8c394e4f-1154-5d85-9535-8a7a4b1a9b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251736} {:answer/id #uuid "9180c1c8-1f7c-540a-8d44-d585577c0e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251795} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f59c7d-fd33-58d7-ae00-8babf85da183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} :answer-field/id #uuid "e38d674a-89c9-50fe-9a20-d74c11c871f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253196}] :question/id #uuid "0c7b9ea7-cded-56a3-a2f3-1334f92c0300" :question/math-academy-id "q-11726" :question/problem "If $P=\\begin{bmatrix}n & -8 \\\\ -2 & n\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ n & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0752f8-54df-507a-872b-fce6c55fcc41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259989} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8f8217-73b8-5aac-bc6a-21c690404158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260111} {:answer/id #uuid "a0659982-c103-5f57-83fb-988b62210ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261268} {:answer/id #uuid "a7949e65-d752-55be-b89d-fa6d51459350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261338} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb45516-48e8-5a7d-bb41-07e91dbcf8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261268} :answer-field/id #uuid "de18e845-9fc1-5af4-bf61-8d1ea6725965" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262509}] :question/id #uuid "524e74d6-0355-574f-af8e-7809bad3676c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127899" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k-1 & k-1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(k-1)\\cdot (-1)-(k-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-k+1-3k+3 \\\\  & =-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0c10c6-3508-5550-98fd-f098d04bede5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260141} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8f1f21-9c81-5ef5-b4fe-0d20d66954ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260426} {:answer/id #uuid "66ed762d-bc10-5c9a-9a0d-59b6f60da393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260773} {:answer/id #uuid "beafacad-b185-562e-8397-0f520d94cd1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261557} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bf894e-96f1-598c-861b-46bd6ece34bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260426} :answer-field/id #uuid "909985c8-f2ff-5344-aacb-a238867289fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262379}] :question/id #uuid "49be873f-6aae-5fe9-b9e9-08cc0609f50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127900" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k & 3 \\\\ 27 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot k-27\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-81 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ k & =\\pm 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=\\pm 9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0694821e-0afc-5a6f-9ac3-c60009288f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259936} {:answer/id #uuid "82ad1107-f4f2-56fb-a170-26080bfb5a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261009} {:answer/id #uuid "93eed24a-7d3e-5252-8646-ba1e56d6756f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261161} {:answer/id #uuid "acb60d02-9af1-5edb-8a62-0a7f615d8394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261386} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b9c926-8614-5473-84ac-a0af3c07259f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f9163f-3e19-52b4-9fae-e228093cfe55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262453}] :question/id #uuid "54a4b93b-d93e-5ce6-98ac-7b0ed79d28ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-127901" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & a \\\\ a & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =48\\cdot 3-a\\cdot a \\\\  & =144-{a}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}144-{a}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =144 \\\\ a & =\\pm 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $a$ are $a=\\pm 12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e10364-a8ca-5a9b-8ec9-fb274ee07c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259910} {:answer/id #uuid "64215484-b9df-5191-b8c1-9280990fe3aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260740} {:answer/id #uuid "b5950187-60d8-50ca-a7cc-6a821b22c615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261470} {:answer/id #uuid "cec39778-4048-5806-ae58-6218823c031b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261705} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a62acf-b03a-52a7-ab5a-7633988a7413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261470} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfd7d4c7-e60d-5c53-95c8-2c7046132a9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262488}] :question/id #uuid "a4d5dba8-4e64-55e3-a838-e85b88eeb6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-127903" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 5 \\\\ t & 9\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 9-t\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =9t-5t \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3059120f-ca9e-51ca-9841-1f8df800e6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260311} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf24db5-f1ae-5524-83bc-edf5d3ad239e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260659} {:answer/id #uuid "621ece07-1998-5006-b429-8870d6c0b314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260720} {:answer/id #uuid "673bf1ec-9954-5f5f-b4e0-082e19a5ab7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260777} {:answer/id #uuid "929a515e-de47-5de2-b043-79d260b71667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261149} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e9e066-1c72-5b37-a693-dbbf75cdc32f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262445}] :question/id #uuid "97157127-f9e4-550a-8517-ce69acd7410c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127905" :question/problem "If $P=\\begin{bmatrix}n & -4 \\\\ -16 & n\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-16)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-64 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =64 \\\\ n & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "327c9e3e-2327-51e3-ab75-0eb4d6685f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260330} {:answer/id #uuid "5528c44b-359f-5f31-ae64-915cc0634cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260602} {:answer/id #uuid "919764a7-f044-599d-84f6-09b075397514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261140} {:answer/id #uuid "97871f23-59b7-5612-bd45-e5666681499e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261190} {:answer/id #uuid "f0dc053c-ee76-590f-8164-11bfcb310e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260330} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e938186-12f9-50c6-849c-59f9dee1509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262236}] :question/id #uuid "14d76c92-61a7-5867-aa92-05e432da7958" :question/math-academy-id "q-127906" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 2 \\\\ t & -8\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot (-8)-t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8t-2t \\\\  & =-10t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fba74c9-a43c-555d-83a0-5e97204b4777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291171} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea8202f6-c433-5f73-acb4-de5dcc90eb03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292470}] :question/id #uuid "2f93a0ad-99aa-54d9-bd35-c1d6b3dc5f05" :question/math-academy-id "q-275738" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}x-5 & x+3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-5)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (x+3) \\\\  & =-3x+15-2x-6 \\\\  & =-5x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f094e6ec-5f6f-5194-9357-eb5f114fc97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296547} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a06ad97-49ee-5366-b8f2-4bd5dbd655a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c475049-0b34-568a-8379-75689981b1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295611} :answer-field/id #uuid "58394d53-5ee7-54cb-8c01-d51839d9b8d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296813}] :question/id #uuid "e8e1210d-36f7-5324-a441-3fe5324d9d56" :question/math-academy-id "q-313957" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}x-4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & x+2\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-4)\\cdot (x+2)-7\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-8-7 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-15 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2c8819-78f4-5fff-bc17-cec5c19efd38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298086} :answer-field/id #uuid "b790ef95-1954-53e9-951c-93434ba44d92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299257}] :question/id #uuid "95d2a0a0-79cd-50d5-95db-d0f4cfda76fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-316781" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 5x-1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (5x-1) \\\\  & =-4x+4-20x \\\\  & =-24x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24x+4 & =0 \\\\ 24x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "892579b6-7828-5a0d-ab85-d5b77ff9a388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298147} :answer-field/id #uuid "e05f6368-cb27-51a1-9aa0-8c61326772fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299398}] :question/id #uuid "0e69fc32-4426-5cb8-9829-2fc1f8cd28fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316782" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f65bbf81-a8fe-5107-aa3e-22d11d717c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298604} :answer-field/id #uuid "635dc510-988f-5cfd-b2b9-b02500ed4e94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298971}] :question/id #uuid "a90dc1ce-cf3a-57f1-9a32-63fe824c4a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-316783" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}5x & -1 \\\\ 6x-8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(5x)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (6x-8) \\\\  & =10x+6x-8 \\\\  & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16x-8 & =0 \\\\ 16x & =8 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c35d1a75-f277-5a94-961c-420517cab2dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298410} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee21428-abe9-5f94-b753-8373c581c767" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299065}] :question/id #uuid "1bc74342-0f37-5e04-9085-a552735d6bba" :question/math-academy-id "q-316784" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -x+1 \\\\ 5 & 2x+7\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(-3)\\cdot (2x+7)-5\\cdot (-x+1) \\\\  & =-6x-21+5x-5 \\\\  & =-x-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-26 & =0 \\\\ -x & =26 \\\\ x & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04cca41b-96b6-5473-9aca-86b0db2b84ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d3dd1b-e2db-5caf-ae0b-809e4a9c8547" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298811}] :question/id #uuid "6d52bc53-4740-5cbf-85a5-c4eda2c297f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316785" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7x-3 & x+8\\end{bmatrix}$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (x+8)-(-2)\\cdot (7x-3) \\\\  & =4x+32+14x-6 \\\\  & =18x+26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18x+26 & =0 \\\\ 18x & =-26 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{13}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "629ba2fb-f7a0-55ec-8318-3a578b3a696d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297974} :answer-field/id #uuid "0facb49d-44d7-596b-8283-cf6ecd88d19e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b84a7230-bf17-5af7-b714-634c6fe7a61b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298353} :answer-field/id #uuid "2558d65a-fb7e-502b-9124-c77726154021" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298762}] :question/id #uuid "113042b9-3913-565d-9ff6-26aa252c490f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316825" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x+4 & 0 \\\\ 15 & -x-3\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+4)\\cdot (-x-3)-0\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-6x-4x-12 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-10x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+5x+6) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5366c8ee-0f20-52a8-af0d-6262c3e3a64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297903} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d33276a-59ca-5611-8a71-d122c8fe1aa8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d68a03-e244-5376-9981-66b7a4ebd931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef19e34-416f-58ea-9adf-3a70138385ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298743}] :question/id #uuid "5a81a924-c8d9-5da7-9d7c-338e9d3bb52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-316828" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2x+1 & x-40 \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+1)\\cdot (-x)-(x-40)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-x-x+40 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-2x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-2x+40 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+x-20) & =0 \\\\ -2(x-4)(x+5) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd68271a-9473-595e-b5cc-3fdbfc5ed8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298378} :answer-field/id #uuid "91c07df3-718b-531d-bfd7-b454f78a656b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab82d06-28db-5541-b1f2-29ddc998b877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297608} :answer-field/id #uuid "e11d6092-7929-53ab-a1f3-28dc7122ce6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299403}] :question/id #uuid "e6886658-7f8f-54c1-b88e-4ea7a22c6205" :question/math-academy-id "q-316829" :question/problem "Let $B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -x+7 \\\\ x-5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3\\cdot 0-(-x+7)\\cdot (x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-5x-7x+35 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-12x+35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+35 & =0 \\\\ (x-7)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =7,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f0d1eb-63da-516d-b39c-98936ea702c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336248} {:answer/id #uuid "3e475449-d5a0-5355-9040-0c60f6ed7506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336619} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8e773e-5ecc-5ed1-a6ae-65cce087450b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336734} {:answer/id #uuid "94bf4718-c6d0-59d1-9ec4-b22670dd22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337391} {:answer/id #uuid "96bb9ff0-d964-5085-8a7c-e0e55abb0c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337403} :answer-field/id #uuid "01585e92-cf9f-5695-8971-52db4143edc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338280}] :question/id #uuid "1f42b909-72e3-5c68-a789-fc35f80e300c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71967" :question/problem "If $V=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & y \\\\ 5 & y\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1608f206-6cae-571f-8d1e-16b6d162d46d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336238} {:answer/id #uuid "287ca0dc-331e-527d-b8c0-e766a590d0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1fd271-6941-56e0-8167-86c17416a68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337323} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e027a-7384-58dc-b2bb-94433e7f22eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337473} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f32404-27a9-5015-979f-c6987e1fe3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336411} :answer-field/id #uuid "53c72237-b3c8-5418-adbd-d5b4558f878e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338421}] :question/id #uuid "d71eb817-7b8e-5d55-9dca-4bfa26de23cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71968" :question/problem "If $H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f062ffd-0731-5c9d-b5df-1e280483ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336623} {:answer/id #uuid "87e8b87b-9219-5612-bc47-0727af4eb0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1a9b12-eb65-52f2-be17-471977096571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337454} {:answer/id #uuid "db1521d6-6365-5c27-8635-662375c34db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337942} {:answer/id #uuid "e0112779-824d-50fa-a23d-b42b80a0e397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337259} :answer-field/id #uuid "82b667e3-83f0-533b-abd1-94355475f197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338510}] :question/id #uuid "35c7dc25-96f0-5d9f-9d6a-dfbf5fcfb320" :question/math-academy-id "q-71969" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Variable in a Singular Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 864 :topic/title "Inverses of 2x2 Matrices"}]}
